{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1773939567,"nonce":"yycTUwZlP4hcIbNulTPaGGNW4wc=","message":"**Three-agent ToS compliance audit (2026-03-19)**\n\nIndependent audits by Opus (x2) and Gemini Flash against Anthropic's current policies (Consumer Terms, Commercial Terms, AUP, SDK docs, Legal \u0026 Compliance page at code.claude.com).\n\n**Key policy source**: code.claude.com/docs/en/legal-and-compliance explicitly states: 'OAuth authentication (used with Free, Pro, and Max plans) is intended exclusively for Claude Code and Claude.ai. Using OAuth tokens obtained through Claude Free, Pro, or Max accounts in any other product, tool, or service — including the Agent SDK — is not permitted.'\n\n**Consensus findings**:\n- OAuth reuse (local/personal): Fine per Anthropic employee Thariq's public clarification\n- OAuth reuse (distributed): Non-compliant — explicit prohibition (unanimous)\n- Conversation history import (JSONL parsing): Compliant — local files, user owns data (unanimous)\n- SDK wrapping (claude-agent-sdk): Compliant — explicitly supported use case (unanimous)\n- Auth queue / git-bug: N/A — no Anthropic involvement\n- Branding ('Mandible'): Compliant — distinct name\n\n**New technical finding**: `settingSources: ['user', 'project', 'local']` in sdk-backend.ts may cause the SDK to automatically pick up Claude Code's consumer credentials via fallback. This is the specific mechanism to block for public release — either require ANTHROPIC_API_KEY explicitly or remove settingSources.\n\n**Additional action items for public release**:\n1. Block OAuth fallback (require API key or remove settingSources)\n2. Scrub git history of OAuth setup instructions (already in scope)\n3. Add README disclaimer: requires API key, not affiliated with Anthropic\n4. Note proprietary SDK dependency ('All rights reserved') in license docs\n5. Consider contacting Anthropic sales proactively (invited on their Legal page)\n\n**'Open Claw' context**: Real incident (Jan-Feb 2026). Anthropic deployed server-side blocks for non-official OAuth clients. News coverage: The Register (Feb 20), Winbuzzer (Feb 19), PiunikaWeb (Feb 19). Enforcement targets distributors, not personal/local use.","files":null}]}